            "review_title": "Review at Chay Au Lac",
            "review_text": "Christina E\nBarcelona, Spain1 contribution\n0\nBest find in Da Nang\nApr 2015 • Couples\nWe were looking for something else, when I saw the yellow \"chay\" sign pointing down a small alley. I checked it out and asked the very nice owner for prices and what time she closed (just had lunch, so we weren't hungry). Came back later in the day for dinner, and had a wonderful meal, which we unfortunately were too hungry to stop and take pictures of.\n\nThe place is very clean, the food inexpensive, and although the owner doesn't speak much English, she's easy to communicate with. There is a small menu with English translations, besides the mock meat in the display. For com tam we paid 30.000d each. \n\nThere's a homey feeling about the place - and they welcomed us with open arms when we came in, soaking wet from the rain. There's an upstairs as well, but we didn't see it.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 22, 2015",
